1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emigrerade 1887-06-23 till Kulm, North Dakota, USA.
2 CONT Hon tar barnens efternamn Jonson och hon blir allmänt kallad Bakmar Jonson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bakmar Jonson came to the United States in 1887 from Norejo [Norsjo], Vasterbotten lan, Sweden with three daughters and two sons.
2 CONT Bakmar homesteaded in Swede Township and lived there until she was unable to care for herself.  She made her home with her daughter Mrs. John Bjur until her death in February of 1914.
2 CONT The children who are all deceased were: Charlie, Erick, Ida, Mrs. August Carlson; Wilhelmina,
2 CONT Mrs. Jacob Bjur; Hulda; Adeline, Mrs. John Bjur. 
2 CONT One son and one daughter stayed in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ur en skrift "History of Kulm ND 1892-1957.doc"
