1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kråken 12
2 CONT
2 CONT Birger Sjöström writes: Mårten "was then 18 years old and 5 feet and eight inches long [173cm] and served as a soldier during an unusually long time. In 1774, he resigned and was 43 years, with 26 years of service and was dismisse
2 CONC d with a pension because he had his own farm."
2 CONT
2 CONT "During his service, Mårten Olofsson Vippa had taken part in the Pomeranian War (1757--1762 several times. He was commanded to Pomerania in August 1757, Rügen January 1759, Bissdorf November 1759, Löiz November 1760 and Gribbnow D
2 CONC ecember 1761. Amazingly, he survived the war and continued as a soldier until 1774. He died on September 1, 1800 in Bodbyn, Burträsk parish. Mårten Olofsson Vippa was probably born in Bursiljum, Burträsk parish in 1730, married in
2 CONC  1751 to Sara Jacobsdotter, born in 1734 in Lappvattnet (same parish). Mårten and Sara had eight children of whom the eldest was born before marriage. For a long time the family was living in Mjödtjärnliden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His service record shows that "Soldat Mårten Olofsson-Hwippa" served under the Västerbotten regiment Lövånger's company, rote 13, Burträsk parish. His service record: "Enlisted 1748: 18 years 1/3 tj.-year. Wästerbottning unmarried
2 CONC ." (from https://forum.rotter.se/index.php?topic=37947.0 )
