1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Bjur was born in Sweden August 7, 1870, the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Jonas Johnson. 
2 CONT She received her schooling and lived in Sweden until she was 17 when she came to America and settled north of Kulm.
2 CONT She was united in marriage to Jacob Bjur in a little school house in Swede Township on November 13, 1892. 
2 CONT They farmed in the community until her husband passed away, October 8, 1935.
2 CONT Following Mr. Bjur's death, Mrs. Bjur lived with her youngest son, Stanley. 
2 CONT Mrs. Bjur passed away on December 3, 1956.
2 CONT Two children preceded Mrs. Bjur in death. The four living children are: Mrs. Horace Blackford, 
2 CONT Effa, of Auburn, Calif.; Caleb, Alvin, and Stanley of Kulm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ur en skrift "History of Kulm ND 1892-1957"
